  "problem": "If $A$ is true, then $A\u21d2B$ is{{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "The statement $A\u21d2B$ is true *unless* $A$ is true and $B$ is false. \n\nLet's break this down into cases:\n\n- When $A=\\text{T}$ and $B=\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A\u21d2B) & \u2261(\\text{T}\u21d2\\text{T}) \\\\  & \u2261\\text{T}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $A=\\text{T}$ and $B=\\text{F},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A\u21d2B) & \u2261(\\text{T}\u21d2\\text{F}) \\\\  & \u2261\\text{F}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $A$ is true, then $A\u21d2B$ is $\\text{sometimes true}.$\n\nThe complete truth table for $A\u21d2B$ is shown below:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A\u21d2B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |",
